OL,3,GNEWSAPumpkin patches see a bright side
OL,4,Ato scorching summer
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe hot, dry summer may have led to
OL,7,Fscorched fields and smaller crop yields
OL,8,F- but pumpkin farmers have welcomed
OL,9,Fbigger, more colourful produce in time
OL,10,Ffor Halloween.
OL,12,F"There's probably a few less pumpkins
OL,13,Fper plant this year than some years,"
OL,14,Fsays Jen Barker, who runs Yorkshire
OL,15,FPumpkins with her husband Rob.
OL,17,FThe couple, who are based Cundall near
OL,18,FThirsk, have produced this year's crop
OL,19,Fwithout external irrigation which has
OL,20,Faffected their total yield.
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
